  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This issue still persists in 1205, with the new SDK in the unity editor. This issue occurs in the unity editor but also ingame.\n\nCollission were ticked off, angle limits were disabled for testing - they actually help in limiting from moving in that far away, but it still gets stuck in the off-rotation.\n\nAll PhysBone transforms in a chain seem to spaz out, when you scale the Y-axis of its root bone. In the example I'm scaling a hair bone. If it's higher than ~1.25 Y scale, the hair starts to behave weirdly by seemingly rotating outwards after any movement and being stuck in said angle instead of going back to the original rotation. It can still move around, but will always be off-angle. This also gets worse with higher Y scales, up to a 90° angle.\nIf it's being scaled lower than 1.0, e.g. 0.7 and smaller, it'll instead not move at all or just spaz out as in they all get stuck at the max angle limit of its parent or up to 90° if there's no angle limit. It also moves so fast that it basically flickers inbetween those absurd angles.\n\nIf you don't scale the root bone but scale the child bones, the issue does seem to be fixed - but not if the root bone get's scaled. This is especially noticeable if the bone chain only has 1 bone (e.g. bangs) or other things like bones with little weightpaint for some slight jiggles (think of thigh bones), and then scaling those up - issue on collision.\n\nShowcasing the issue (no sound):\nhttps://youtu.be/d4h8PlyFBw8\n\nA secondary, related issue using the thigh example: when the thigh is being scaled up on the Y-Axis and a collider enters it's collision radius, the thigh bone would spaz out and rapidly flicker inbetween different angles, not coming to a rest even if the collider were to move away.",
